  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows volatility or a downward trend; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 3-6 EUR.",
    "When sentiment history contains mixed signals (e.g., +1.00 and -1.00) or low values, the model fails to capture mean reversion, predicting steady growth instead of oscillation.",
    "Forecasts show significant lag in reacting to sudden price spikes; true outcomes often reach new highs within 3-5 days while models remain flat for weeks.",
    "In volatile regimes (history range >10 EUR), the model's linear extrapolation creates a 'smoothness bias,' underestimating the frequency of sharp corrections seen in true data.",
    "Sentiment spikes (+1.00) do not correlate with forecast increases; models ignore sentiment entirely, relying solely on historical averages which are often outdated."
  ]
}
